This wildcard A record makes **every** hostname under `jeremysitlab.com` resolve to `10.5.0.4` (srv1's own IP). Confirmed: `pc1.jeremysitlab.com`, `pc2.jeremysitlab.com`, `pc3.jeremysitlab.com`, `laptop1.jeremysitlab.com` — all return `10.5.0.4` instead of their real IPs. DNS is up and answering; it's answering *wrongly* for every name except `srv1` itself.

